---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Adalar: a day trip from Heya · HeyaGuide"
  description="How to spend a perfect day on Büyükada and Heybeliada — the Princes' Islands in the Sea of Marmara. Ferry tips, phaeton loop, Aya Yorgi hike, where to eat."
>
  <article class="trip">
    <div class="trip-hero">
      <img src="/trips/adalar-hero.jpg" alt="Aya Yorgi Monastery on Büyükada" />
    </div>

    <header class="trip-head container">
      <p class="trip-eyebrow">Day trip from Heya</p>
      <h1>Adalar: a day on the Princes' Islands</h1>
      <p class="trip-lede">
        The Princes' Islands (Adalar) are Istanbul's other world — a car-free
        archipelago in the Sea of Marmara where you trade traffic horns for
        phaeton bells, pine forests for minarets, and the Bosphorus for the
        wide blue of the Marmara. The classic day is on Büyükada, with
        Heybeliada as the quieter alternative.
      </p>
      <div class="trip-meta">
        <div class="trip-meta-item">
          <span class="trip-meta-label">From Heya</span>
          <span class="trip-meta-value">~2 h 30 min door to door</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trip-meta-item">
          <span class="trip-meta-label">Total day</span>
          <span class="trip-meta-value">6–8 hours on the islands</span>
        </div>
        <div class="trip-meta-item">
          <span class="trip-meta-label">Best for</span>
          <span class="trip-meta-value">A full day, or two half-days</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="trip-body container">
      <p class="trip-lede-2">
        The 9 islands of the Adalar archipelago sit about 20 km southeast
        of the city. Four are open to visitors; the largest and most
        popular is Büyükada, with Heybeliada, Burgazada, and Kınalıada as
        progressively quieter alternatives. Cars have been banned since
        2020, so the transport on the islands is the traditional phaeton
        (horse-drawn carriage), a rental bike, or your own two feet.
      </p>

      <h2>The morning: ferry out, get your bearings</h2>
      <p>
        Leave Heya at about 9 a.m. Take the F1 funicular to Kabataş, walk
        the 5 minutes to the Kabataş ferry terminal, and board a Şehir
        Hatları ferry to Büyükada. They leave every 1–2 hours, take 75 to
        105 minutes depending on which boat you catch, and are Istanbulkart
        (use your top-up card, ~₺60 each way). Sit on the right side
        coming back, the left side going out — the Bosphorus views are
        better on those sides.
      </p>
      <p>
        The ferry threads past the old city, the Topkapı skyline, the
        Maiden's Tower, the Bosphorus entrance, and then opens out into the
        Marmara. You'll pass the other three islands on the way in. Around
        11 a.m. the ferry docks at the Büyükada pier, a small chaotic
        waterfront with phaeton drivers calling out, fish restaurants, and
        bicycle rental stalls.
      </p>

      <h2>Late morning: the phaeton or bike loop</h2>
      <p>
        The classic first move is the <strong>island loop</strong> — an
        11 km paved road that circles the perimeter of the island, going
        clockwise past the Yörükali pine forest in the centre. Two
        options:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Phaeton (₺200–400 for the full loop, negotiate at the
          pier)</strong> — the open-topped, horse-drawn carriage that's
          the most famous Adalar experience. The horses are well-cared-for
          at the licensed stands; avoid the unlicensed touts on the
          waterfront.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Rental bike (₺50–100 per hour)</strong> — a more
          flexible option; you'll stop when you want, and the central
          pine forest is only accessible by bike or on foot.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The loop takes about 2 hours without stops, but budget 3 hours
        for the regular photo stops: the wooden Ottoman mansions on the
        north side, the view of the Marmara from the western cliffs, and
        the <a href="/places/buyukada">Aya Yorgi Monastery</a> parking lot
        at the top of the south hill, where the phaeton lets you off and
        the walking route to the monastery begins.
      </p>

      <h2>Lunch: fish at the waterfront, or a taverna inland</h2>
      <p>
        After the loop, you'll be back at the pier area by about 2 p.m.
        The waterfront has a string of fish restaurants, all of them
        decent and all of them tourist-priced. The classic order is
        grilled mackerel (levrek izgara) and a small meze plate. Total
        for two with a drink: ~₺400–600.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you want a more local feel, walk 5 minutes inland up the main
        hill road to one of the small tavernas on the back streets. They
        get more local customers and have the same fish for less.
      </p>

      <h2>Mid-afternoon: Aya Yorgi Monastery, or the pine-forest walk</h2>
      <p>
        After lunch you have two choices. The first is the
        <strong>Aya Yorgi hike</strong>: from the phaeton drop-off, walk
        up the cobbled path (about 20 minutes) to the small Greek Orthodox
        monastery at the top of the south hill. There's a wishing tree
        and an iron wishing well (tie a piece of cloth, drop a coin).
        The view from the top, with both the Marmara and the old-city
        skyline behind you, is the best on the island.
      </p>
      <p>
        The second option, if you've had enough uphill, is the
        <strong>pine-forest walk</strong> in the centre of the island: a
        45-minute loop through the trees, mostly flat, mostly shaded,
        with picnic tables. Good for families with small kids.
      </p>

      <h2>Late afternoon: the ferry back, or stop at Heybeliada</h2>
      <p>
        The last Büyükada ferry back to Kabataş leaves around 6 p.m. in
        summer and 4–5 p.m. in winter. If you've had a leisurely day and
        don't want the rush, an alternative is to take the inter-island
        ferry to <a href="/places/heybeliada">Heybeliada</a> for an hour
        or two — the Halki Theological School, the Naval Cadet School,
        and a quieter waterfront — then catch the Kabataş ferry from
        Heybeliada pier.
      </p>
      <p>
        You'll be back at Heya by about 7:30 p.m. (or 8:30 if you came
        via Heybeliada), which leaves time for a quiet dinner in Beyoğlu
        — we can recommend a few places if you ask at the desk.
      </p>

      <h2>Practicalities</h2>
      <ul class="trip-practical">
        <li><strong>What to wear:</strong> whatever you're comfortable in. Shorts and t-shirts are fine. The only constraint is the Aya Yorgi Monastery: modest dress (covered shoulders, knees) if you want to go inside.</li>
        <li><strong>What to bring:</strong> sunscreen, sunglasses, water, a hat if you're fair. There's a small supermarket on the pier if you want to grab water for the day.</li>
        <li><strong>Cash:</strong> most phaeton drivers and some restaurants are cash-only. There are ATMs on the pier.</li>
        <li><strong>If it rains:</strong> the day is largely a bust. The phaeton doesn't run in heavy rain and the walk to Aya Yorgi is slippery. Save the trip for a clear day.</li>
        <li><strong>Best months:</strong> May, June, September, October. July and August are very hot. November–March is cold and many of the waterfront restaurants close.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Related places</h2>
      <ul class="trip-related">
        <li><a href="/places/buyukada">Büyükada</a> — the main island, with the Aya Yorgi hike and phaeton loop</li>
        <li><a href="/places/heybeliada">Heybeliada</a> — the greenest island, quieter, with the Halki seminary view</li>
        <li><a href="/places/burgazada">Burgazada</a> — the smallest, the sleepiest, Sait Faik's island</li>
        <li><a href="/places/kinaliada">Kınalıada</a> — the closest to the Asian side, swimming and quiet</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .trip {
    background: var(--color-bg-elevated);
  }

  .trip-hero {
    aspect-ratio: 21/9;
    max-height: 420px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-bg-muted);
  }

  .trip-hero img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .trip-head {
    padding: var(--space-8) var(--container-pad) var(--space-6);
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .trip-eyebrow {
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wider);
    color: var(--color-brand);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .trip-head h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .trip-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .trip-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
    justify-content: center;
    padding: var(--space-4) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .trip-meta-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }

  .trip-meta-label {
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wider);
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .trip-meta-value {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .trip-body {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding: var(--space-7) var(--container-pad) var(--space-9);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .trip-lede-2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .trip-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    margin: var(--space-7) 0 var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .trip-body p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .trip-body ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
  }

  .trip-body li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .trip-body a {
    color: var(--color-brand);
  }

  .trip-practical li {
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .trip-practical strong,
  .trip-related strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .trip-related {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
  }

  .trip-related li {
    padding: var(--space-2) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .trip-related li:first-child,
  .trip-related li:nth-child(2) {
    border-top: none;
  }

  .trip-related a {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .trip-hero {
      aspect-ratio: 4/3;
      max-height: 280px;
    }
    .trip-related {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
